}
class "processing.lifecycle" as Life <<module>> $PROC {
 claim(factory, job_id, attempt_id, settings)
 live(pair, token, now)
 heartbeat(factory, work, settings)
 finish(factory, work, *, outputs, error)
}
Claim -[hidden]right- Life
Life ..left> Claim : claim() creates;
Life ..right> Cleanup : cleanup_intent()
note bottom of Claim
  Claim is local worker authority; never a queue payload.
  Frozen fields; nested dict/list remain mutable.
  Lease is Attempt columns, not a Lease class.
  V1 legacy source_url is empty; Source descriptor is used.
end note
note bottom of Cleanup
  Per Attempt: 0..1 intent; per Job: 0..* intents.
  job_id + attempt_id are local FKs.
  finish(error), retry, cancel, interrupt:
  stage intent; recovery scans attempt prefix.
end note
legend bottom
  Dashed = dependency, not composition. IDs refer to existing Job / Attempt, not object pointers.
  lock_pair() + live() fence heartbeat / finish; SQL does not enforce the whole state machine.
endlegend

